    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106401" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδρό-εις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εσσα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fond of the water,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόναξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					349
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.):— <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑδροῦσσα</span> was a name of the island Tenos (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ τὸ κατάρρυτον εἶναι</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				595
			</span></i>, and of an island near Attica, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.1.21
			</span></i>.</div>
